"""Benchmark: prompt volume generated by the EvoMe fast + slow paths (LONG reply).

This is a companion to `benchmark_token_cost.py`. The only behavioral
difference is the fake model: instead of the project `FakeLLM`'s 9-character
reply, it returns a realistic-length deterministic Chinese answer of ~2328
characters (the measured average of the user's real assistant responses).

Why a second script?

The Phase 5.7C truncation (`EVOME_PROMPT_RESPONSE_CHAR_LIMIT`, default 1200)
only fires when the assistant response is longer than the budget. With the
original 9-character fake reply it never fires, so its effect on prompt volume
is invisible. This script makes the truncated portion of the prompt measurable.

What it measures
----------------
- Every call the runtime makes through its LLM adapter: the fast-path answer
  plus the slow-path gates / post-turn assessor / context builder / reflection /
  relation judge.
- For each call: the inferred purpose (using the same
  `DeepSeekClient._infer_purpose` markers the production client uses), the
  method name, and the total number of characters across all message contents.

Limitations
-----------
- It counts *prompt characters*, not billed tokens. No tokenizer is applied and
  provider pricing, output tokens, caching and retries are ignored. Use it for
  relative comparison only (e.g. cadence 1 vs 2, truncation on vs off).
- The slow path is driven to completion after each turn via
  `wait_for_background`, which is stricter than production (production does not
  block on the slow job). Call volume per turn is unaffected by this.
- Qdrant retrieval is bypassed because the runtime is backed by an in-memory
  SQLite database (same behavior as the pytest fixtures); Qdrant does not make
  LLM calls, so this does not affect prompt volume.

Safety
------
- Never opens the real `evome.db`: an in-memory SQLite database is used and
  `EVOME_DB_URL` / `EVOME_QDRANT_PATH` are redirected to temporary locations
  before the app modules are imported.
- No existing project file is modified. This script is additive on purpose.

Usage
-----
    .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe scripts\\benchmark_token_cost_long.py [num_turns]

    # simulate the OLD behavior (no truncation, every turn)
    $env:EVOME_SLOW_LOOP_EVERY_N_TURNS=1; $env:EVOME_PROMPT_RESPONSE_CHAR_LIMIT=100000
    .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe scripts\\benchmark_token_cost_long.py

    # truncation only
    $env:EVOME_SLOW_LOOP_EVERY_N_TURNS=1; $env:EVOME_PROMPT_RESPONSE_CHAR_LIMIT=1200
    .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe scripts\\benchmark_token_cost_long.py

    # cadence only
    $env:EVOME_SLOW_LOOP_EVERY_N_TURNS=2; $env:EVOME_PROMPT_RESPONSE_CHAR_LIMIT=100000
    .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe scripts\\benchmark_token_cost_long.py

    # both (the new default)
    $env:EVOME_SLOW_LOOP_EVERY_N_TURNS=2; $env:EVOME_PROMPT_RESPONSE_CHAR_LIMIT=1200
    .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe scripts\\benchmark_token_cost_long.py

Set them as process environment variables so they override `.env`.
"""

